    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Follicular adenoma, spindle type",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Follicular adenomas of the thyroid gland may undergo spindle cell change, as seen in this example. The nuclei are elongated, as is the cytoplasm. The cells are reactive for thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1 (TTF1), PAX8, and thyroglobulin (not shown).",
    "source": "Lester D.R. Thompson",
    "copyright": "",
